{"orgCode":"5195","name":"1991 State-Local Realignment","agencyCode":"4000","agencyName":"Health and Human Services","description":"In the 1991-92 fiscal year, State-Local Program Realignment restructured the state-county partnership by giving counties increased responsibilities and funding for a number of health, mental health, and social services programs. This realignment provides counties with dedicated tax revenues from the state sales tax and vehicle license fee to pay for these programs.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":7438417,"cy":7634773,"by":7882717},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0}},"programs":{"id":"exp/4000/5195","kind":"department","name":"1991 State-Local Realignment","code":"5195","amounts":{"py":7438417,"cy":7634773,"by":7882717},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":7438417,"cy":7634773,"by":7882717}},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/5195/4350","kind":"program","name":"State-Local Realignment","code":"4350","amounts":{"py":7438417,"cy":7634773,"by":7882717},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":7438417,"cy":7634773,"by":7882717}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"description":"4350 - STATE-LOCAL REALIGNMENT\n\nThe objectives of Realignment are to assign program responsibility to the most appropriate level of government and achieve improved service levels with broad discretion given to the responsible entity. Realignment provides for greater funding stability for selected programs, increased local flexibility in administering these programs, and productive fiscal incentives to encourage cost-effective approaches to providing services.\n\nTotal Realignment revenues are comprised of a half cent sales tax and a dedicated portion of vehicle license fee revenues. Revenues are deposited into the Local Revenue Fund, which includes several accounts. Funds deposited in these accounts are continuously appropriated for allocation to local governments according to formula and are used to fund programs specified in realignment legislation. The legislation also includes local maintenance of effort and matching requirements in order to ensure that counties do not use the realigned funds to supplant local expenditure levels prior to realignment. This provision ensures compliance with other state and federal statutes which, in turn, provide hundreds of millions of dollars annually for county health and social services programs.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":7438417,"cy":7634773,"by":7882717}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/5195/4350/f0329","kind":"fund","name":"Vehicle License Collection Account, Local Revenue Fund","code":"0329","amounts":{"py":14000,"cy":14000,"by":14000},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":14000,"cy":14000,"by":14000}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":14000,"cy":14000,"by":14000}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/5195/4350/f0351","kind":"fund","name":"Mental Health Subaccount, Sales Tax Account","code":"0351","amounts":{"py":339629,"cy":339629,"by":339629},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":339629,"cy":339629,"by":339629}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":339629,"cy":339629,"by":339629}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/5195/4350/f0352","kind":"fund","name":"Social Services Subaccount, Sales Tax Account","code":"0352","amounts":{"py":2521108,"cy":2521108,"by":2615966},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":2521108,"cy":2521108,"by":2615966}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":2521108,"cy":2521108,"by":2615966}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/5195/4350/f0353","kind":"fund","name":"Health Subaccount, Sales Tax Account","code":"0353","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":76686,"by":54787},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":0,"cy":76686,"by":54787}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":0,"cy":76686,"by":54787}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/5195/4350/f0354","kind":"fund","name":"Caseload Subaccount, Sales Tax Growth Account","code":"0354","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":94858,"by":1